course: dictionary
lesson: 7522
title: Practically: almost, or in real life?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Practically often means almost or nearly. «The jar is practically empty» means there is very little left, but not none. Check by swapping in almost: «The jar is almost empty» still makes sense, so practically means almost here.
explain: Practically can also mean in a sensible, useful, real-life way. «Think practically about what to pack» means choose the things you will really need, not just the things you like. The words around the word show you which meaning fits.
explain: A third meaning is in practice, as things really are, not in theory. Phrases such as «practically speaking» and «practically nothing» help you hear it. When you meet practically, ask: does almost fit? If yes, it is probably the first meaning.
fact: Practically means almost or nearly, as in «The jar is practically empty.»
fact: Practically can mean in a sensible, useful, real-life way, as in «Think practically about what to pack.»
fact: Practically can also mean in practice, as things really are, not in theory.
fact: «The Great Wall of China is practically impossible to see with the naked eye from orbit (circling the Earth in space), astronauts report.»
fact: Common phrases with practically include «practically nothing», «practically everyone» and «practically speaking».
exercise: «The jar is practically empty.» What does practically mean here? | Slowly | Loudly | *Almost | Sensibly
exercise: «Think practically about what to pack for the trip.» What does practically mean here? | Happily | *In a sensible, useful, real-life way | Loudly and clearly | Almost
exercise: «The gold coins practically completed the matter.» Which word could replace practically? | Quietly | Happily | Badly | *Nearly
test: Mum says «practically everyone came to the party». What does practically mean here? | Everyone, sensibly and carefully | *Almost everyone | Only one person | No one at all
test: «Practically speaking, we should take the bus.» What does practically mean here? | Almost | Unhappily | Loudly | *In a sensible, real-life way
exam: Which use of practically means almost? | Practical plans for lunch | Think practically about the trip | Practically speaking, we should walk | *The jar is practically empty
